A simple cmavo thus has the property of having only one or two vowels, or
of having a single consonant followed by one or two vowels. Words
consisting of three or more vowels in a row, or a
single consonant followed by three or more vowels, are also of cmavo form,
but are reserved for experimental use: a few examples are ``ku'a'e'',
``sau'e'', and ``bai'ai''. All CVV cmavo beginning
with the letter ``x'' are also reserved for experimental use.




